WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:03.010
How closely will "Uncharted" stick to the
games?

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:04.010
Who's starring?

00:00:04.010 --> 00:00:05.049
What's the story?

00:00:05.049 --> 00:00:07.660
And most importantly, when can we watch it?

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:10.670
Here's everything you need to know about "Uncharted."

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:13.420
Cinema's influence on video games cannot be
denied.

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:17.520
From the mountains upon mountains of game
adaptations to the medium's fingerprint on

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:23.270
the direction and writing of games, movies
have a large hand in shaping games as an art form.

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:27.140
Some games, of course, are more movie-like
than others, and few studios are as successful

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:29.640
at making cinematic games as Naughty Dog.

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:33.570
With mega-popular titles like "The Last of
Us" and its sequel wearing their cinematic

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:38.440
influences on their sleeve, the company has
built its reputation as the premier cinematic

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:40.160
game developer in the world.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:44.350
The shoe is about to be on the other foot,
however, as we get closer and closer to Sony's

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:48.550
film adaptation of Naughty Dog's action-adventure
series, "Uncharted."

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:53.100
The "Uncharted" film has had a long and troubled
production history riddled with delays but

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:56.420
has finally seemed to find its stride in the
past year or so.

00:00:56.420 --> 00:01:01.149
Now, it seems reasonably certain that "Uncharted's"
most recent release date will be final.

00:01:01.149 --> 00:01:03.399
Here is what we know so far.

00:01:03.399 --> 00:01:08.140
Sony first went public with their plans for
an "Uncharted" movie all the way back in 2008.

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:13.330
Since then, there has been no end to the number
of production hurdles pushing back the film's actual release.

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:17.920
In the midst of more than a few rewrites,
recasts, and director pass-offs, Sony first

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:20.740
announced a theatrical release for 2016.

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:26.130
Not long afterward, the release was moved
to one date after the other, including 2017,

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:33.300
March 2021, July 2021, October 2021, and February
2022.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:36.770
After a certain point, it seemed as if "Uncharted"
would never be released.

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:41.370
However, after 13 years and seven different
directors, it seems as if the movie has reached

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:47.990
the light at the end of the tunnel: The "Uncharted"
movie will premiere in theaters on February 18, 2022.

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:52.450
One of the biggest draws for the upcoming
"Uncharted" film are its two talented co-stars.

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:57.530
The original "Uncharted" game series focused
on the adventures of scruffy treasure hunter/thief

00:01:57.530 --> 00:02:01.710
Nathan Drake and his suave hustling mentor,
Victor "Sully" Sullivan.

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:05.479
Originally, the role of Nathan Drake was supposed
to go to Mark Wahlberg.

00:02:05.479 --> 00:02:11.019
However, after a number of rewrites, Sony
decided to focus on a younger version of the character.

00:02:11.019 --> 00:02:15.340
They then gave the role of Nathan Drake over
to "Spider-Man: Homecoming" star Tom Holland.

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:18.700
However, Sony wasn't about to push Marky Mark
to the sidelines.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:24.299
The benefit of telling a story about a young
Nathan Drake is that Sully is also a bit more youthful.

00:02:24.299 --> 00:02:29.409
This opened the way for Wahlberg to step in
and assume the role of Drake's seedy father figure.

00:02:29.409 --> 00:02:32.189
Of course, nothing is so simple when it comes
to this movie.

00:02:32.189 --> 00:02:36.349
Fans have had mixed feelings about some of
the film's casting decisions, especially with

00:02:36.349 --> 00:02:37.579
regard to Sully.

00:02:37.579 --> 00:02:42.599
Holland could make a convincing younger Drake,
but Wahlberg as Sully would take some convincing.

00:02:42.599 --> 00:02:47.079
This is especially true after rumors circulated
that this Sully might not have his iconic

00:02:47.079 --> 00:02:50.059
mustache for the entire duration of the film.

00:02:50.059 --> 00:02:53.209
Evidently, a stache-less Sully is akin to
heresy.

00:02:53.209 --> 00:02:56.880
Still, many fans remain optimistic about the
film's starring duo.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.819
"What is that thing on your face?"

00:02:59.819 --> 00:03:01.700
"Puberty is right around the corner, kid.

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:03.540
You can grow your own."

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:09.269
The rest of the main cast includes: Antonio
Banderas, who will be playing Santiago Moncada,

00:03:09.269 --> 00:03:14.481
the heir to a wealthy and powerful house that
once lost a fabled fortune; Sophia Ali, who

00:03:14.481 --> 00:03:18.919
will be playing Chloe Frazier, Nathan Drake's
longtime love interest who first appeared

00:03:18.919 --> 00:03:25.959
in "Uncharted 2"; and Tati Gabrielle, who
plays Braddock, a mercenary working against Nathan and Sully.

00:03:25.959 --> 00:03:30.109
Sony Pictures has released an official synopsis
for the "Uncharted" movie, which reads:

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:34.859
"Street-smart Nathan Drake is recruited by
seasoned treasure hunter Victor 'Sully' Sullivan

00:03:34.859 --> 00:03:41.639
to recover a fortune amassed by Ferdinand
Magellan and lost 500 years ago by the House of Moncada."

00:03:41.639 --> 00:03:43.219
So far, so "Uncharted."

00:03:43.219 --> 00:03:44.529
The synopsis continues,

00:03:44.529 --> 00:03:49.340
"What starts as a heist job for the duo becomes
a globe-trotting, white-knuckle race to reach

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:55.120
the prize before the ruthless Santiago Moncada,
who believes he and his family are the rightful heirs."

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:59.599
With the villain introduced — a perfectly
cast Antonio Banderas — the synopsis concludes,

00:03:59.599 --> 00:04:04.069
"If Nate and Sully can decipher the clues
and solve one of the world's oldest mysteries,

00:04:04.069 --> 00:04:09.359
they stand to find $5 billion in treasure
and perhaps even Nate's long-lost brother...but

00:04:09.359 --> 00:04:11.969
only if they can learn to work together."

00:04:11.969 --> 00:04:16.699
Based on the plot summary, it sounds like
the movie will be very much in line with the video games.

00:04:16.699 --> 00:04:20.700
Most games in the "Uncharted" series starts
off with Drake and Sully hunting for treasure

00:04:28.622 --> 00:04:31.052
a circumnavigation of the planet.

00:04:31.052 --> 00:04:35.462
Without fail, this leads Drake and Sully on
a wild goose chase rife with artifacts and

00:04:35.462 --> 00:04:39.962
mysteries until he discovers some lost city
or vast repository of treasure.

00:04:39.962 --> 00:04:43.932
Based on what we know about these versions
of Drake and Sully, we can determine that

00:04:43.932 --> 00:04:48.918
the film will take place prior to the main
plotlines of any of the original "Uncharted" games.

00:04:48.918 --> 00:04:53.452
However, the film likely won't be a straight-up
origin story, as the events regarding Drake

00:04:53.452 --> 00:04:58.402
and Sully's initial encounter were covered
during flashback portions of "Uncharted 3."

00:04:58.402 --> 00:05:02.252
Based on the trailers, it looks like "Uncharted"
will mine the games for action set pieces

00:05:02.252 --> 00:05:06.742
and Easter eggs, and will likely be more of
an homage to the games than a missing chapter

00:05:06.742 --> 00:05:08.712
in their larger story.

